        "id": 1128369
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-09-08T01:34:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "we can discharge disable in deferred function with only this change in BD99955.c\nif (interrupts \u0026 BD99955_CMD_INT_SET_TH_RES \u0026\u0026\n    vbus \u003c BD99955_VBUS_DISCHARGE_TH)\n    pd_set_vbus_discharge(bd99955_pd_port_to_chg_port(port))",
      "revId": "67c874d65e35330869869634c0196cdf1f3458d7",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f68dffb6_ff69d220",
        "filename": "board/kevin/usb_pd_policy.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 72,
      "author": {
        "id": 1001696
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-09-08T21:40:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t understand, can you explain your comment more? Are you suggesting that we can disable discharge if VBUS level is below 4V, regardless of whether we\u0027re sourcing it or not?",
      "parentUuid": "f68dffb6_400d90eb",
      "revId": "67c874d65e35330869869634c0196cdf1f3458d7",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f68dffb6_9f4e0e86",
        "filename": "board/kevin/usb_pd_policy.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 72,
      "author": {
        "id": 1128369
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-09-08T21:53:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes correct. And also we can avoid BD99955_CMD_INT_SET_TH_DET interrupt.",
      "parentUuid": "f68dffb6_ff69d220",
      "revId": "67c874d65e35330869869634c0196cdf1f3458d7",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f68dffb6_7f24e2bc",
        "filename": "board/kevin/usb_pd_policy.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 72,
      "author": {
        "id": 1001696
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-09-08T21:57:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think we can avoid using this interrupt. Ignoring source cases (only acting as a sink), we still need to enable discharge at some point (to ensure we don\u0027t end up at intermediate voltage where VBUS is still detected, yet we aren\u0027t charging) and we also need to disable it at some point (to ensure charger efficiency).",
      "parentUuid": "f68dffb6_9f4e0e86",
      "revId": "67c874d65e35330869869634c0196cdf1f3458d7",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
